{"Zero-length override comparison uses reference equality on two newly-created Dayjs objects instead of value comparison, so empty date overrides meant to block availability don't work": 0.917673647403717, "When a slot falls inside a date override, the code returns available before calendar busy checks run, allowing double-booking even when there's an existing busy block during the override window": 0.8341137170791626, "Working hours guard rejects a slot when any same-day working-hours row does not contain it, causing valid slots in split schedules (like 09:00-12:00 and 13:00-17:00) to be incorrectly rejected": 0.9318457841873169, "A slot that starts exactly at the date override end is incorrectly accepted because the check only rejects starts after the end, not at the end boundary": 0.6574282050132751, "Mixed timezone DST correction issue where override minutes are normalized with override.timeZone but buildSlots still applies DST corrections from event organizerTimeZone, causing override windows to shift by an hour in certain timezone combinations": 0.6649646162986755}